1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
One component, one path, one dataset: follow the continuity of the examination.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Large blade roots transfer loads to the rotor. This case examines the first groove, where access is constrained by the geometry and adjacent blades. Study case: plan and explain the search for indications in a difficult access area.

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:44,000
A traceable examination helps locate, characterise and compare indications. Interpretation supports maintenance decisions together with applicable criteria and service data. Simulation and a reconstructed image alone do not establish fitness for service.

4
00:00:44,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Link the component, scanner, path, signals, maps and report in one coordinate framework. C1 and C2 present complementary access configurations for the root. This demonstration replays source responses; no physical acquisition is connected.

5
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Compare successive examinations and create controlled variants for learning. Retain settings, uncertainties and the origin of every root state. Successive-state monitoring is an objective to demonstrate, not an already validated industrial monitoring capability.

6
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Three blades: show root access and identify the groove to be examined.

7
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Two shells and a carriage: a design study linked to the examination path.

8
00:01:48,000 --> 00:02:04,000
The section links the support face, probe position and target area.

9
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Selected positions from one replay: geometry, mapping and signal remain synchronised.

10
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Selected positions from one replay: geometry, mapping and signal remain synchronised.

11
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Selected positions from one replay: geometry, mapping and signal remain synchronised.

12
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Compare the EDM references and results from the same dataset.

13
00:02:46,000 --> 00:03:04,000
A reconstruction helps interpret responses; it does not replace true geometry.

14
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Distinguish the reconstructed image from the actual flaw shape and volume.

15
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Report and exports: link observations to the case references and parameters.

16
00:03:40,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Predict the response, observe the signal, compare C1 and C2 access, then explain the interpretation. An EDM reference is a test reference, not an identical in-service crack. Learning goal: understand why an indication is visible, weak or masked.

17
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:20,000
UT results → flaw model and uncertainty → crack geometry → loading and material → mechanical assessment. TFM or voxel image extent does not directly establish the mechanical crack size.

18
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Reference state → next examination or simulated variant → documented comparison → hypothesised flaw evolution → mechanical reassessment. Current applications do not compute validated criticality or service life. This link remains to be developed.

19
00:04:40,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Define the conditions → propose variants → compute responses using a suitable model → check consistency → compare consequences. Development perspective: AI proposes hypotheses; validated scenario generation is not demonstrated here.

20
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Compare successive states and document their origin: the next step to demonstrate.

21
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Plan → execute → interpret → retain → compare. BYTE NDT — Living Engineering.
